## The term-graph view of a typed graph: nodes are subterms, sharing is explicit, children are inline (a tree with symbolic cross-links). graphToTermGraph builds it; schemaToTypeGraph is the type-side twin. Term graphs are Ariola-Klop's nested systems of recursion equations.
module hydra.core.subterms

import hydra.core.errors as errors
import hydra.core.extract.model as extract.model
import hydra.core.graph as graph
import hydra.core.lib.eithers as eithers
import hydra.core.lib.equality as equality
import hydra.core.lib.lists as lists
import hydra.core.lib.logic as logic
import hydra.core.lib.maps as maps
import hydra.core.lib.optionals as optionals
import hydra.core.lib.pairs as pairs
import hydra.core.lib.sets as sets
import hydra.core.lib.strings as strings
import hydra.core.model as model
import hydra.core.paths as paths
import hydra.core.reflect as reflect
import hydra.core.rewriting as rewriting
import hydra.core.substitution as substitution

## The expected type to thread into an immediate child, given this node's (synthesized) type, its term, and the step reaching the child. This is the term->type position map underlying the TermGraph:TypeGraph erasure: element positions get the container element type, mapEntry gets pair<K,V>, lambdaBody the codomain, and so on. `none` where the child's type is not fixed top-down (e.g. a function-position subterm), which is fine for non-empty children.
term expectedForStep = λschema,typ,`term`,step.let elementOfList := λt.cases(model.Type){`list`=λe.given(e), `_`=none} t in let elementOfSet := λt.cases(model.Type){`set`=λe.given(e), `_`=none} t in let elementOfOptional := λt.cases(model.Type){`optional`=λe.given(e), `_`=none} t in let codomainOf := λt.cases(model.Type){function=λft.given(model.FunctionType[codomain] ft), `_`=none} t in let mapPairType := λt.cases(model.Type){`map`=λmt.given(model.Type{pair = model.PairType{first = model.MapType[keys] mt, second = model.MapType[values] mt}}), `_`=none} t in cases(paths.SubtermStep){listElement=λ`_`.elementOfList typ, setElement=λ`_`.elementOfSet typ, optionalGiven=λ`_`.elementOfOptional typ, lambdaBody=λ`_`.codomainOf typ, mapEntry=λ`_`.mapPairType typ, pairFirst=λ`_`.cases(model.Type){pair=λpt.given(model.PairType[first] pt), `_`=none} typ, pairSecond=λ`_`.cases(model.Type){pair=λpt.given(model.PairType[second] pt), `_`=none} typ, recordField=λfname.fieldTypeFromSchema schema `term` fname, injectField=λfname.fieldTypeFromSchema schema `term` fname, `_`=none} step

## The expected type of a record field / injected union field, from the named type in the schema
term fieldTypeFromSchema = λschema,`term`,fname.cases(model.Term){`record`=λr.optionals.bind (maps.lookup (model.Record[typeName] r) schema) (λsty.eithers.either (λ`_`.none) (λfields.findFieldTypeIn fname fields) (extract.model.recordType (model.Record[typeName] r) sty)), `inject`=λinj.optionals.bind (maps.lookup (model.Injection[typeName] inj) schema) (λsty.eithers.either (λ`_`.none) (λfields.findFieldTypeIn fname fields) (extract.model.unionType (model.Injection[typeName] inj) sty)), `_`=none} `term`

## The type of the named field within a list of field types, if present
term findFieldTypeIn = λfname,fields.optionals.map model.FieldType[`type`] (lists.head (lists.filter (λf.equality.equal (model.FieldType[name] f) fname) fields))

## The term-graph view of a typed graph: one root node per binding. Sharing is explicit; children are inline (a tree); variable occurrences become symbolic references carrying their binding node's id. Input must be a POST-INFERENCE (elaborated) graph: binding schemes present, lambda domains present, typeLambda/typeApplication explicit. Node types are synthesized in one O(n) bidirectional pass; a missing annotation (or an untyped empty leaf) is a precondition failure.
term graphToTermGraph = λgraph.let boundTerms := graph.Graph[boundTerms] graph in let schema := maps.map (λts.model.TypeScheme[body] ts) (graph.Graph[boundTypes] graph) in eithers.map (λroots.paths.TermGraph{roots = maps.fromList roots}) (eithers.mapList (λnt.let name := pairs.first nt in let `term` := pairs.second nt in let expected := rootExpectedType schema name in eithers.map (λnode.(name, node)) (termGraphNode graph schema name maps.empty sets.empty expected paths.SubtermPath{[]} `term`)) (maps.toList boundTerms))

## The expected type for a root binding node: its declared type in the schema, if present
term rootExpectedType = λschema,name.maps.lookup name schema

## The type-graph view of a schema: one root node per named type. A Type.variable referencing a schema-bound name is a nominal reference; a forall-bound variable in scope is a variable reference to its binding node; leaf types and non-type constituents are carried as links.
term schemaToTypeGraph = λschema.let schemaNames := maps.keys schema in eithers.map (λroots.paths.TypeGraph{roots = maps.fromList roots}) (eithers.mapList (λnt.let name := pairs.first nt in let typ := pairs.second nt in eithers.map (λnode.(name, node)) (typeGraphNode (sets.fromList schemaNames) name maps.empty paths.SubtypePath{[]} typ)) (maps.toList schema))

## Synthesize the type of an elaborated subterm, syntax-directed and without unification, threading `expected` top-down. Reads annotations (lambda domain, typeApplication type) and combines child types bottom-up; synthesis-incomplete leaves (empty list/set/map, optional none, either's absent branch) CONSUME `expected`. `expected = none` at such a leaf is a precondition failure with path.
term synthesizeType = λgraph,schema,env,root,expected,path,`term`.let recurseInto := λmexp,child.synthesizeType graph schema env root mexp path child in let fail := λmsg.left(errors.Error{other = errors.OtherError{strings.concat2 (strings.concat2 "synthesizeType precondition: " msg) (strings.concat2 " at " (model.Name[] root))}}) in let consumeExpected := λwhat.optionals.match expected (fail (strings.concat2 "untyped " what)) (λt.right(t)) in let elementOfExpected := optionals.bind expected (λt.cases(model.Type){`list`=λe.given(e), `set`=λe.given(e), `optional`=λe.given(e), `_`=none} t) in let codomainOfExpected := optionals.bind expected (λt.cases(model.Type){function=λft.given(model.FunctionType[codomain] ft), `_`=none} t) in cases(model.Term){application=λapp.eithers.bind (recurseInto none (model.Application[function] app)) (λftype.cases(model.Type){function=λft.right(model.FunctionType[codomain] ft), `_`=fail "application of a non-function"} ftype), lambda=λl.optionals.match (model.Lambda[domain] l) (fail "lambda without a domain annotation") (λdom.eithers.map (λbt.model.Type{function = model.FunctionType{domain = dom, codomain = bt}}) (recurseInto codomainOfExpected (model.Lambda[body] l))), typeLambda=λtl.eithers.map (λbt.model.Type{`forall` = model.ForallType{parameter = model.TypeLambda[parameter] tl, body = bt}}) (recurseInto none (model.TypeLambda[body] tl)), typeApplication=λta.eithers.bind (recurseInto none (model.TypeApplicationTerm[body] ta)) (λbt.cases(model.Type){`forall`=λft.right(substitution.substInType (substitution.singletonTypeSubst (model.ForallType[parameter] ft) (model.TypeApplicationTerm[`type`] ta)) (model.ForallType[body] ft)), `_`=fail "type application of a non-forall"} bt), variable=λname.optionals.match (maps.lookup name env) (optionals.match (maps.lookup name schema) (fail (strings.concat2 "unbound variable " (model.Name[] name))) (λt.right(t))) (λt.right(t)), `unit`=λ`_`.right(model.Type{`unit`}), literal=λlit.right(model.Type{literal = reflect.literalType lit}), `optional`=λmt.optionals.match mt (consumeExpected "optional none") (λt.eithers.map (λx.model.Type{`optional` = x}) (recurseInto elementOfExpected t)), `list`=λels.optionals.match (lists.head els) (consumeExpected "empty list") (λt0.eithers.map (λx.model.Type{`list` = x}) (recurseInto elementOfExpected t0)), `set`=λs.optionals.match (lists.head (sets.toList s)) (consumeExpected "empty set") (λt0.eithers.map (λx.model.Type{`set` = x}) (recurseInto elementOfExpected t0)), `map`=λm.optionals.match (lists.head (maps.toList m)) (consumeExpected "empty map") (λkv.eithers.bind (recurseInto none (pairs.first kv)) (λkt.eithers.map (λvt.model.Type{`map` = model.MapType{keys = kt, values = vt}}) (recurseInto none (pairs.second kv)))), pair=λp.eithers.bind (recurseInto none (pairs.first p)) (λft.eithers.map (λst.model.Type{pair = model.PairType{first = ft, second = st}}) (recurseInto none (pairs.second p))), `either`=λe.consumeExpected "either value", `record`=λr.optionals.match (maps.lookup (model.Record[typeName] r) schema) (fail (strings.concat2 "record type not in schema: " (model.Name[] (model.Record[typeName] r)))) (λt.right(t)), `inject`=λinj.optionals.match (maps.lookup (model.Injection[typeName] inj) schema) (fail (strings.concat2 "union type not in schema: " (model.Name[] (model.Injection[typeName] inj)))) (λt.right(t)), `wrap`=λw.optionals.match (maps.lookup (model.WrappedTerm[typeName] w) schema) (fail (strings.concat2 "wrapper type not in schema: " (model.Name[] (model.WrappedTerm[typeName] w)))) (λt.right(t)), annotated=λat.recurseInto expected (model.AnnotatedTerm[body] at), `let`=λlt.recurseInto expected (model.Let[body] lt), `project`=λp.let tname := model.Projection[typeName] p in let fname := model.Projection[fieldName] p in optionals.match (maps.lookup tname schema) (fail (strings.concat2 "projection type not in schema: " (model.Name[] tname))) (λsty.eithers.bind (extract.model.recordType tname sty) (λfields.optionals.match (findFieldTypeIn fname fields) (fail (strings.concat2 "projected field not in record type: " (model.Name[] fname))) (λftyp.right(model.Type{function = model.FunctionType{domain = model.Type{variable = tname}, codomain = ftyp}})))), `unwrap`=λtname.optionals.match (maps.lookup tname schema) (fail (strings.concat2 "unwrap type not in schema: " (model.Name[] tname))) (λsty.eithers.map (λinner.model.Type{function = model.FunctionType{domain = model.Type{variable = tname}, codomain = inner}}) (extract.model.wrappedType tname sty)), `cases`=λcs.let tname := model.CaseStatement[typeName] cs in let rep := optionals.match (model.CaseStatement[default] cs) (optionals.map model.CaseAlternative[handler] (lists.head (model.CaseStatement[`cases`] cs))) (λd.given(d)) in optionals.match rep (fail "case statement with no branches") (λhandler.eithers.bind (recurseInto none handler) (λhtype.eithers.map (λft.model.Type{function = model.FunctionType{domain = model.Type{variable = tname}, codomain = model.FunctionType[codomain] ft}}) (extract.model.functionType htype))), `_`=fail "unsupported term constructor"} `term`

## The content attribute links contributed by a term constructor (a non-term constituent, with its value)
term termAttributesOf = λ`term`.cases(model.Term){`cases`=λcs.[paths.TermAttributeLink{casesTypeName = model.CaseStatement[typeName] cs}], `inject`=λinj.[paths.TermAttributeLink{injectTypeName = model.Injection[typeName] inj}], lambda=λl.lists.concat2 [paths.TermAttributeLink{lambdaParameter = model.Lambda[parameter] l}] (optionals.match (model.Lambda[domain] l) [] (λd.[paths.TermAttributeLink{lambdaDomainGiven = d}])), literal=λlit.[paths.TermAttributeLink{literal = lit}], `project`=λp.[paths.TermAttributeLink{projectTypeName = model.Projection[typeName] p}, paths.TermAttributeLink{projectFieldName = model.Projection[fieldName] p}], `record`=λr.[paths.TermAttributeLink{recordTypeName = model.Record[typeName] r}], typeApplication=λta.[paths.TermAttributeLink{typeApplicationType = model.TypeApplicationTerm[`type`] ta}], typeLambda=λtl.[paths.TermAttributeLink{typeLambdaParameter = model.TypeLambda[parameter] tl}], `unwrap`=λu.[paths.TermAttributeLink{unwrapTypeName = u}], `wrap`=λw.[paths.TermAttributeLink{wrapTypeName = model.WrappedTerm[typeName] w}], `_`=[]} `term`

## Build a term-graph node (inline) for the subterm at the given path within a root binding. `env` maps each in-scope local variable to its (binder node id, type); `lambdaScope` marks the lambda-bound subset. `expected` is the type flowing top-down, consumed by synthesis-incomplete leaves. A variable child is not a node: the parent emits a reference link for it.
term termGraphNode = λgraph,schema,root,env,lambdaScope,expected,path,`term`.let steps := paths.SubtermPath[] path in let thisId := paths.TermNodeId{root = root, path = path} in let envTypes := maps.map (λp.pairs.second p) env in let childEnv := cases(model.Term){lambda=λl.maps.insert (model.Lambda[parameter] l) (thisId, optionals.withDefault model.Type{variable = model.Name{"?"}} (model.Lambda[domain] l)) env, `let`=λlt.lists.foldl (λacc,b.let bname := model.Binding[name] b in let bid := paths.TermNodeId{root = root, path = paths.SubtermPath{lists.concat2 steps [paths.SubtermStep{letBinding = bname}]}} in let btype := optionals.withDefault model.Type{variable = model.Name{"?"}} (optionals.map model.TypeScheme[body] (model.Binding[typeScheme] b)) in maps.insert bname (bid, btype) acc) env (model.Let[bindings] lt), `_`=env} `term` in let childLambdaScope := cases(model.Term){lambda=λl.sets.insert (model.Lambda[parameter] l) lambdaScope, `_`=lambdaScope} `term` in eithers.bind (synthesizeType graph schema envTypes root expected path `term`) (λtyp.let attrLinks := lists.map (λx.paths.TermLink{attribute = x}) (termAttributesOf `term`) in eithers.bind (eithers.mapList (λst.let step := pairs.first st in let child := pairs.second st in let childPath := paths.SubtermPath{lists.concat2 steps [step]} in let childExpected := expectedForStep schema typ `term` step in cases(model.Term){variable=λname.eithers.map (λref.paths.TermLink{reference = paths.TermReferenceLink{step = step, target = ref}}) (termReferenceFor graph childEnv childLambdaScope name), `_`=eithers.map (λcnode.paths.TermLink{subterm = paths.SubtermLink{step = step, child = cnode}}) (termGraphNode graph schema root childEnv childLambdaScope childExpected childPath child)} child) (rewriting.subtermsWithSteps `term`)) (λchildLinks.right(paths.TermNode{`term` = `term`, `type` = typ, links = lists.concat2 attrLinks childLinks})))

## Classify a variable occurrence, carrying its binder's node id: lambda-bound (node = the binding lambda), let-bound — locally or as a graph binding — (node = the bound term), or a primitive; a free variable is a precondition failure. `lambdaScope` marks which local names are lambda-bound.
term termReferenceFor = λgraph,env,lambdaScope,name.optionals.match (maps.lookup name env) (logic.ifElse (maps.member name (graph.Graph[boundTerms] graph)) right(paths.TermReference{`let` = paths.LetVariableReference{variable = name, bindingNode = paths.TermNodeId{root = name, path = paths.SubtermPath{[]}}, `type` = optionals.withDefault model.Type{variable = model.Name{"?"}} (optionals.map model.TypeScheme[body] (maps.lookup name (graph.Graph[boundTypes] graph)))}}) (logic.ifElse (maps.member name (graph.Graph[primitives] graph)) right(paths.TermReference{`primitive` = paths.PrimitiveReference{name = name, `type` = model.Type{variable = model.Name{"?"}}}}) left(errors.Error{other = errors.OtherError{strings.concat2 "free variable in term graph: " (model.Name[] name)}}))) (λidType.let binderId := pairs.first idType in let occType := pairs.second idType in logic.ifElse (sets.member name lambdaScope) right(paths.TermReference{lambda = paths.LambdaVariableReference{variable = name, boundByNode = binderId, `type` = occType}}) right(paths.TermReference{`let` = paths.LetVariableReference{variable = name, bindingNode = binderId, `type` = occType}}))

## The content attribute links contributed by a type constructor: annotation, forall parameter, or literal type
term typeAttributesOf = λtyp.cases(model.Type){annotated=λat.[paths.TypeAttributeLink{annotatedAnnotation = model.AnnotatedType[annotation] at}], `forall`=λft.[paths.TypeAttributeLink{forallParameter = model.ForallType[parameter] ft}], literal=λlt.[paths.TypeAttributeLink{literal = lt}], `_`=[]} typ

## Build a type-graph node (inline) for the subtype at the given path within a named root type
term typeGraphNode = λschemaNames,root,forallScope,path,typ.eithers.map (λlinks.paths.TypeNode{`type` = typ, links = links}) (typeLinks schemaNames root forallScope path typ)

## The outgoing links of a type node: its content attributes, and one link per immediate subtype — a variable occurrence becomes a reference link on the parent (occurrences are not nodes), any other subtype an inline subtype link. `forallScope` maps each in-scope forall variable to its binding node id.
term typeLinks = λschemaNames,root,forallScope,path,typ.let steps := paths.SubtypePath[] path in let thisId := paths.TypeNodeId{root = root, path = path} in let attrLinks := lists.map (λx.paths.TypeLink{attribute = x}) (typeAttributesOf typ) in let childScope := cases(model.Type){`forall`=λft.maps.insert (model.ForallType[parameter] ft) thisId forallScope, `_`=forallScope} typ in eithers.bind (eithers.mapList (λst.let step := pairs.first st in let child := pairs.second st in let childPath := paths.SubtypePath{lists.concat2 steps [step]} in cases(model.Type){variable=λname.eithers.map (λref.paths.TypeLink{reference = paths.TypeReferenceLink{step = step, target = ref}}) (typeReferenceFor schemaNames childScope name), `_`=eithers.map (λcnode.paths.TypeLink{subtype = paths.SubtypeLink{step = step, child = cnode}}) (typeGraphNode schemaNames root childScope childPath child)} child) (rewriting.subtypesWithSteps typ)) (λchildLinks.right(lists.concat2 attrLinks childLinks))

## Classify a type variable occurrence: a schema-bound name is a nominal reference; a forall-bound variable in scope is a variable reference carrying its binding forall's node id; anything else is a free-variable precondition failure.
term typeReferenceFor = λschemaNames,forallScope,name.logic.ifElse (sets.member name schemaNames) right(paths.TypeReference{nominal = paths.NominalTypeReference{name = name}}) (optionals.match (maps.lookup name forallScope) left(errors.Error{other = errors.OtherError{strings.concat2 "free type variable in type graph: " (model.Name[] name)}}) (λbinderId.right(paths.TypeReference{variable = paths.TypeVariableReference{variable = name, boundByNode = binderId}})))